(1606108, 215055, 35804, '<td valign="top">I think maybe there is a word missing from the title? (not?)...I think this is what confused me...1776-Freedom of, NOT from, a state of religion...that makes total sense. I like images that try to say something...that get the ole'' blood boiling, or atleast make people think...the more I look at this the more I like it, esp. how the cross appears "separated" from the building bring about the whole separation of state and church issue...again "of " not "from"...I''ll be looking forward to seeing the other comments this image might get. The dark sky is such a nice contrast against the lightness of the building and cross.</td>', 'I think maybe there is a word missing from the title? (not?)...I think this is what confused me...1776-Freedom of, NOT from, a state of religion...that makes total sense. I like images that try to say something...that get the ole'' blood boiling, or atleast make people think...the more I look at this the more I like it, esp. how the cross appears "separated" from the building bring about the whole separation of state and church issue...again "of " not "from"...I''ll be looking forward to seeing the other comments this image might get. The dark sky is such a nice contrast against the lightness of the building and cross.', '2005-08-12 12:32:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1606125, 215717, 35804, '<td valign="top">...you know... I just really like this... I keep coming back to this image...the light and shadow are just so appealing...I love the yellow...it really is a "slice" of life, so vernacular really. I used to take pictures like this when I was younger...my early 20''s and younger and my mother thought I was nuts..."Why are you taking a picture of your messy room?" ( Actually, now that I tihnk about it, I still take pictures of my messy rooms.) I would even elaborately light the mess with studio lighting... and looking back at them now I find them quite fascinating...and so does my mom....sorry to ramble and I hope you aren''t getting tons of hateful comments for not fitting the challenge...I really like this, I like it alot.</td>', '...you know... I just really like this... I keep coming back to this image...the light and shadow are just so appealing...I love the yellow...it really is a "slice" of life, so vernacular really. I used to take pictures like this when I was younger...my early 20''s and younger and my mother thought I was nuts..."Why are you taking a picture of your messy room?" ( Actually, now that I tihnk about it, I still take pictures of my messy rooms.) I would even elaborately light the mess with studio lighting... and looking back at them now I find them quite fascinating...and so does my mom....sorry to ramble and I hope you aren''t getting tons of hateful comments for not fitting the challenge...I really like this, I like it alot.', '2005-08-12 12:44:30.000000', NULL, 1),
