(1616792, 213464, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by macrothing:</b></div><hr/><i> 5 - This shot has been a bit of a quandry for me to comment on.  It is such a great shot in many ways, the foreground, the teepees(sp?), the differing levels of the mountains, the lighting, the cloud, the mist?, I just wish you had only put the year.  In fact to me, this shot without the title tells other stories before the Lewis &amp; Clark one.  Just my opinion, discard it if you wish, I only comment because it IS a great photo.  But for me, it''s all about the Challenge first.  Ok, up to 5 from 4.  Just in my opinion, if you had just the year, it would leave the viewer ''open'' to interpret it in a variety of ways.  Criticism; maybe a different frame, maybe a little less of the fore, but that does add balance, look in MY opinion, it is an excellent shot, just... that ol'' title business that was part of the description and that ''most'' have adhered to.  Definitely an 8 with just the year. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t rank this photo very high either. Nothing against the photo itself just that I didn''t see this as a strong entry for this particular challenge. Luckly for you the majority disagreed :) and felt a shot of teepees fit this era. Interesting shot nonetheless.</td>', 'Originally posted by macrothing: 5 - This shot has been a bit of a quandry for me to comment on.  It is such a great shot in many ways, the foreground, the teepees(sp?), the differing levels of the mountains, the lighting, the cloud, the mist?, I just wish you had only put the year.  In fact to me, this shot without the title tells other stories before the Lewis & Clark one.  Just my opinion, discard it if you wish, I only comment because it IS a great photo.  But for me, it''s all about the Challenge first.  Ok, up to 5 from 4.  Just in my opinion, if you had just the year, it would leave the viewer ''open'' to interpret it in a variety of ways.  Criticism; maybe a different frame, maybe a little less of the fore, but that does add balance, look in MY opinion, it is an excellent shot, just... that ol'' title business that was part of the description and that ''most'' have adhered to.  Definitely an 8 with just the year.   I didn''t rank this photo very high either. Nothing against the photo itself just that I didn''t see this as a strong entry for this particular challenge. Luckly for you the majority disagreed :) and felt a shot of teepees fit this era. Interesting shot nonetheless.', '2005-08-17 03:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1616830, 214206, 41337, '<td valign="top">Looks perfect to me. After voting on all the entries I thought yours had everything. Great photo in general and most important it nails the subject of the challenge. Take away the title and you still know what era you''re conveying. That''s something you can''t say for many of the photos ranked ahead of yours. Good job.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-17 03:11:53.</i></td>', 'Looks perfect to me. After voting on all the entries I thought yours had everything. Great photo in general and most important it nails the subject of the challenge. Take away the title and you still know what era you''re conveying. That''s something you can''t say for many of the photos ranked ahead of yours. Good job.', '2005-08-17 04:11:04.000000', '2005-08-17 04:11:53.000000', 0),
