(1617371, 214596, 15711, '<td valign="top">My only critique would be maybe a tad less shadowing on her face. She certainly depicts a moment in the time period you called it. I always like the subject to be a little off center, but since she takes up the entire shot, it doesn''t affect the quality. Maybe give her a smidge more "headroom."</td>', 'My only critique would be maybe a tad less shadowing on her face. She certainly depicts a moment in the time period you called it. I always like the subject to be a little off center, but since she takes up the entire shot, it doesn''t affect the quality. Maybe give her a smidge more "headroom."', '2005-08-17 09:20:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1617383, 214180, 30049, '<td valign="top">Thanks Scott.  I have the same file cabinet you do.  ;^)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by exbionic:</b></div><hr/><i> I''m stunned.  This should have finished a lot higher.  As usual though, all my opinions can filed under "what the hell do I know?" ;-) </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks Scott.  I have the same file cabinet you do.  ;^) Originally posted by exbionic: I''m stunned.  This should have finished a lot higher.  As usual though, all my opinions can filed under "what the hell do I know?" ;-) ', '2005-08-17 09:23:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1617406, 214521, 33515, '<td valign="top">Thanks Langdon and to everyone for your comments, I updated the story behind the picture in the Photo Comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-17 08:36:02.</i></td>', 'Thanks Langdon and to everyone for your comments, I updated the story behind the picture in the Photo Comments.', '2005-08-17 09:32:25.000000', '2005-08-17 09:36:02.000000', 0),
(1617483, 215565, 39270, '<td valign="top">Just to explain the "folding chairs".  This was a cabin built in 1836 around the area which is now called Grapevine.  It was renovated and transplanted to downtown Grapevine and is now a historical landmarker.  There are live music festivals and that is where the chair''s came into the picture.  At the time I took the picture''s I thought about moving them, but was not sure if we were able.  Now of course I wish I did.<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the votes and comments.  This is by far the most comments I have ever received.</td>', 'Just to explain the "folding chairs".  This was a cabin built in 1836 around the area which is now called Grapevine.  It was renovated and transplanted to downtown Grapevine and is now a historical landmarker.  There are live music festivals and that is where the chair''s came into the picture.  At the time I took the picture''s I thought about moving them, but was not sure if we were able.  Now of course I wish I did. Thanks for all the votes and comments.  This is by far the most comments I have ever received.', '2005-08-17 09:59:19.000000', NULL, 0),
