(1646829, 215697, 25355, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Emilio:</b></div><hr/><i> Great portrait but I don''t think that 1885 AD samurai wore a glove when practicing archery. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That may be true for 1885AD as well as 1185AD. Kyudo (Japanese archery) is immensely difficult and more about the practice and state of mind of it than actually hitting the target. (I tried it once or twice a long time ago.) The thumb piece is actually made of metal covered in deerskin (or something similar).</td>', 'Originally posted by Emilio: Great portrait but I don''t think that 1885 AD samurai wore a glove when practicing archery.   That may be true for 1885AD as well as 1185AD. Kyudo (Japanese archery) is immensely difficult and more about the practice and state of mind of it than actually hitting the target. (I tried it once or twice a long time ago.) The thumb piece is actually made of metal covered in deerskin (or something similar).', '2005-08-26 02:37:01.000000', NULL, 0),
